WEBVTT

00:56:59.417 --> 00:57:02.518
what else is out there
that I haven't yet done

00:57:02.542 --> 00:57:06.518
versus the good enough,
versus the this is rich in and of itself.

00:57:06.542 --> 00:57:09.643
Stay here, deepen it, you know,
build something from it.

00:57:09.667 --> 00:57:10.934
You know, it's just --

00:57:10.958 --> 00:57:14.434
For me, the moment where I read this
was an "Wall Street Journal" article

00:57:14.458 --> 00:57:16.434
that said "The quitters are the winners."

00:57:16.458 --> 00:57:19.601
And I thought, "Oh boy,
one headline tells you what's going on."

00:57:19.625 --> 00:57:21.143
You know, what does it mean?

00:57:21.167 --> 00:57:22.809
And then of course, it explained:

00:57:22.833 --> 00:57:25.059
you get a better salary,
you get promoted more,

00:57:25.083 --> 00:57:29.476
but the whole point was
about leaving versus staying.

00:57:29.500 --> 00:57:31.976
This is, I find I don't --